body:
Yes im using 2 instances of instantsearch.
then in one instance of of them , i implement the searchFunction(helper) like this :

``` javascript
searchFunction: function(helper) {
var query = companiesSearch.helper.state.query;
projectsSearch.helper.setQuery(query);
projectsSearch.helper.search();
helper.search();
}
```

Regarding my index switch, im using a simple form select with 2 options representing my index and then i switch and render the layout accordingly to the selected index using the same input type search, shared by the 2 instances of instantsearch.
